    "body": "Wording and formatting nits.\r\n```suggestion\r\n    <p class=\"note\">Once a start tag with the tag name \"plaintext\" has been seen, all remaining\r\n    tokens will be character tokens (and a final end-of-file token), because there is\r\n    no way to switch the tokenizer out of the <span>PLAINTEXT state</span>. However, as the\r\n    tree builder remains in its existing insertion mode, it might <span>reconstruct the active\r\n    formatting elements</span> while processing those character tokens. This means that it's\r\n    possible for a <code>plaintext</code> element to contain elements.</p>\r\n```",
    "created_at": "2024-08-05T22:14:58Z",
